  "review_items": [
    "Study plot is 7,000 sq ft: 40% above the initial 5,000 sq ft upper target, including a separate right-side pedestrian path beside the ramp. No site or layout approval is implied.",
    "Study 002 expands only the basement from 50 x 80 to 50 x 88 ft: 4,400 sq ft excluding ramp, adding 400 sq ft (10%) toward the front. Above-ground plates remain 2,500 sq ft each; approximately 9,400 sq ft total before detailed deductions.",
    "The basement extends below part of both yards. Lawn/planters above it need structural, waterproofing and drainage review; trees are shown beyond its rear edge.",
    "Ramp central grade is approximately 16.7%; clear width, transitions, SUV swept paths, headroom, protection and flood drainage remain unverified.",
    "Three separate bays and a 25.5 ft aisle are represented, but independent SUV turning has NOT been proven by a swept-path simulation.",
    "Gym/gaming are at the front; stores, toilet and stairs have a protected clean-side route. Rear SUV/motorbike parking is beside the ramp landing, behind an intended full-height sealed barrier and two-door airlock. Walls/doors are shown cut away, not built or certified.",
    "Garage air is to be exhausted independently with appropriate makeup air and negative pressure relative to occupied areas. Separate clean-air ventilation, CO/NO2 controls, fire separation, door swings, egress and commissioning require professional design.",
    "Garage and kitchen exhaust outlets are UNLOCATED: do not discharge into the backyard play lawn, pool/veranda, windows or fresh-air intakes. No fan capacity, duct route or air-quality performance is established.",
    "Garage plant reserve is accessible only from the garage; capacity/equipment remain unresolved. It does not approve LPG, fuel, generator, battery or water-tank placement.",
    "Movable table games are shown in a nominal state; full operating clearances and simultaneous gym/game use need review.",
    "Office swaps with the former front Child 2 room, retains 16 x 16 ft and opens to the shared front balcony. Its private 8 x 5 ft indoor WC has office-only access; nine toilets overall, not a lounge/balcony WC. Laundry stays on ground.",
    "All three children's sleeping rooms increase equally from 16 x 16 to 16 x 17 ft (272 sq ft, +6.25%) within the unchanged 50 x 50 ft first-floor plate. Wardrobe storage moves out of the sleeping rooms into private walk-in dressing areas.",
    "Each child has bedroom -> private walk-in dressing <-> bathroom access. Child 1 dressing is 6.5 x 8 ft and bath 6.5 x 8.5 ft; rear dressing rooms are each 5.5 x 7 ft with 5.5 x 9.5 ft baths. The sleeping rooms are equal; dressing/bath sizes are not identical.",
    "Rear children's bath/dressing zones flank a retained 4 ft common route to the shared rear balcony. The 49 x 9.5 ft seamless lounge/gallery includes shared circulation, not just seating. Front balcony access is through Child 1 or office; rear balcony additionally has common access.",
    "Front and rear balconies are each continuous shared decks without internal privacy screens; perimeter guards remain. The two decks are not a wraparound connection.",
    "Purple parked curtains mark soft bath/dressing dividers; enclosed showers are shown cut away. Curtains alone do not protect clothing from moisture: extraction, waterproofing, humidity control, privacy/locking and detailed plumbing require design review.",
    "Backyard kitchen has a garden-facing sink window, 6 x 3 ft island and indicative cooking hood; mechanical source extraction is required, not replaced by a window. Pantry is directly adjacent.",
    "Living is L-shaped: 14.5 x 21.5 ft outer extents minus a 30 sq ft enclosed pantry = 281.75 sq ft, 34.65% above Study 001's 209.25 sq ft. Prayer remains shared floor space. Dining is 12 x 13.5 ft with an eight-seat 4 x 7.5 ft table.",
    "Guest bathroom dual-door privacy/locking, door swings, master toilet partitions and detailed plumbing need design review.",
    "Pool is outside the main basement rectangle but close to excavation/ramp; structure, access, cover and child-safety barriers need professional review.",
    "Small rooms and furniture are blockouts, not fully resolved cabinetry, appliance or accessible-clearance designs.",
    "Front receiving has an offset route into family space; privacy sightlines, acoustics, glazing, shading and climate performance are not simulated.",
    "Budget feasibility is unverified and the expanded plot, basement and total floor area are significant cost risks.",
    "No plot orientation, legal setbacks, neighbours, soil, groundwater, local permissions or seismic/structural safety have been established.",
    "Optional fishpond and double-height atrium are deferred in this first study. The roof stair head and slab openings are indicative.",
